writeFileSync(resolve(stage,'README.md'),'This is a source-only historical proof migration candidate. Seven existing root verifiers and one new fixed transition module are proposed. No application runtime, tests, registries or published metadata were changed by this stage.\n\nEight named prior source identities map to authenticated immutable beforeimages; installed30, shared85fe and seven current verifier bodies stay mandatory. Historical847/dev117/STATUS b41, API24/named31, Editor Save78/browser31 and Notes/Vault historical references retain original epochs. Six code replacements belonged to old720; SEARCH and Vault README were outside it. The new937/737/753 checkpoint is independently authenticated as separate finite current evidence. Its dev/status identities are not embedded into the migration module, avoiding cyclic metadata pins.\n\nFive source-only filesystem readers pass and24 finite preflight checks pass, including10 mutation rejections. The complete global root publication verifier remains unexecuted here because root owns refreshed publication metadata and actual installation. Child commands only check syntax or proof bytes; app tests/original libraries/GUI/network/benchmarks were not executed.\n\nAll preparation failures and partial-reader observations are retained. Generated private mirrors are excluded from immutable/public payload; their leaf census is an authentication-at-capture record, and read-only hardlinks are not presented as stable historical payload. Redundant current/public acquisition bytes are individually bound to existing public aliases in reused-public-inputs.json instead of copied again. The normal source-only payload and exact verifier beforeimages are frozen by freeze-manifest.json.\n');
for(const p of ['excluded-mirror-census.json','reused-public-inputs.json','live-verifier-copy-list.json','validation.json','README.md'])payload.push({path:p,...id(readFileSync(resolve(stage,p)))});payload.sort((a,b)=>a.path.localeCompare(b.path));
const prefix='products/rea-studio/results/editor-vault-proof-migration-20261013';const publicList=payload.map(r=>({sourcePath:r.path,publicPath:prefix+'/'+r.path+'.snapshot',...r}));for(const r of records.verifiers){const row=publicList.find(p=>p.sourcePath==='verifier-before/'+r.path.slice(8)+'.snapshot');assert(row);row.publicPath=r.historicalPath;}
